{"type":"npc","name":"Ferrofluidic Ooze","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":270,"temp":0,"max":270,"details":""},"ac":{"value":17,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":"magnetic climb"},"immunities":[{"type":"acid","exceptions":[]},{"type":"critical-hits","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]},{"type":"visual","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"piercing","value":10,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":9},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>When an acidic ooze dissolves a large amount of metal, typically iron, it can morph into a ferrofluidic ooze. The churning of the microscopic metal particles within the ooze's gelatinous membranes generates a magnetic field that grants it an unusual physiology. Its smooth black reflective membrane is held together in orderly geometric patterns that it can manipulate. Its endless consumption of metal has rendered its acid ineffective against organic substances, though it can still feed on metal. Like magnetic objects, large amounts of heat can temporarily demagnetize a ferrofluidic ooze.</p><p>These creatures constantly seek out rich metal sources like iron mines, armories, or foundries, posing a threat to blacksmiths and knights alike.</p><h2>Ferrofluid</h2><p>The goop that makes up a ferrofluidic ooze retains its magnetic properties for an hour after the ooze's death. During that time, up to four creatures can apply the ferrofluid to their hands and feet as a 1-minute activity with the manipulate trait. For the next 10 minutes, each creature gains the ferrofluidic ooze's Magnetic Climb ability but is also clumsy 1 for the duration.</p><p>Alternatively, the ferrofluid can be used as one application of <em>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.7IrQPyMm76nLVoXx]</em>, but only to form a bond between two surfaces made of metal. The ferrofluid loses its properties after 1 hour, but if used to bind two metal surfaces, the surfaces remain joined until the bond is broken, typically with a successful @Check[athletics|dc:50] check.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 90/200/360 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), shield, perception item, skill items (Athletics)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (acid, vitality), fortification, metal, strength, sturdy, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Aaron Morder","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":-5},"con":{"mod":7},"int":{"mod":-5},"wis":{"mod":0},"cha":{"mod":-5}},"perception":{"details":"metalsense (imprecise) 60 feet","mod":12,"senses":[{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":false},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":13,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"athletics":{"base":20}},"traits":{"value":["metal","mindless","ooze"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"zM1DZ9vUKsM9oL38","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/ferrofluidic-ooze.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ferrofluidic Ooze","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":2,"height":2,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/ferrofluidic-ooze.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/ferrofluidic-ooze.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"type":"action","name":"Metalsense","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>Due to its innate magnetism, a ferrofluidic ooze senses nearby chunks of metal of at least light Bulk.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"uVHWYhrOh5yjMpJT","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Demagnetize","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>Overwhelming heat can interfere with the ferrofluidic ooze's magnetism. If the ferrofluidic ooze takes 50 or more fire damage at the same time, it temporarily loses its magnetic field. Until the end of its next turn, it loses magnetic attraction, magnetic climb, magnetic coating, magnetic hold, merger, and metalsense.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"6ffxhne2WCt5Suun","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Magnetic Hold","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 10 feet of the ferrofluidic ooze deals slashing damage to it</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ooze splits in half before quickly reforming due to its strong magnetic fields. The ooze attempts an Athletics check to [[/act grapple]] the triggering creature; it does not need to have a free hand to do so. This check neither applies nor counts toward the ferrofluidic ooze's multiple attack penalty.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"IgwwNVXzy7qPXjrS","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Magnetic Attraction","system":{"actionType":{"value":"action"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ferrofluidic ooze manipulates its magnetic field to draw metal toward itself. Each creature within 30 feet that is either wearing metal armor or affected by the ooze's magnetic coating must attempt a @Check[fortitude|dc:25] save. This is forced movement. The forced movement ends once the creature is adjacent to the ooze. Unattended metal objects in the area with a Bulk of 10 or less are automatically drawn 20 feet toward the ooze.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature moves 5 feet toward the ooze.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature moves 10 feet toward the ooze.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature moves 20 feet toward the ooze.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["manipulate","metal","primal"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":1},"category":"offensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"X0N5rJQln33Pxcpp","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Magnetic Climb","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The ferrofluidic ooze can climb on any surface made out of metal, including ceilings and other inverted surfaces, though such surfaces are difficult terrain for it.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["metal","primal"]},"_migrati